Hi Matissa,  

Currently, "lags" creates a lagged version of the original variable (not separated into a series of binary variables). The current value of the "noms" variable is the one that is broken up into a series of binary variables to impute them correctly. To do something more advanced, you may have to create the lags by hand---for instance, with a series of lagged binary indicators of the nominal variable. The same is true for multiple-period lags. 

Hope that helps!

Cheers,
matt.


